{"id": "EUVD-2026-76586", "enisaUuid": "a47da06f-2c94-3523-8c35-4e6aeea9df5f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: fix XDR length calculation in nfsd4_ff_encode_layoutget\n\nThe XDR buffer size calculation in nfsd4_ff_encode_layoutget() has\nmultiple errors that can result in either an out-of-bounds write or\nleaking uninitialized kernel memory to the client:\n\n - fh_len doesn't account for XDR padding on the file handle data\n - uid and gid lengths use \"8 + len\" but xdr_encode_opaque() actually\n   writes \"4 + xdr_align_size(len)\" bytes\n - ds_len omits the flags and stats_collect_hint fields (8 bytes),\n   while len's header constant overestimates by 8 bytes -- these\n   partially cancel but leave a net mismatch\n\nThe worst case occurs with short strings (e.g. uid=0, gid=0 with an\nodd-sized file handle), where the function writes up to 5 bytes past\nthe reserved XDR buffer. Conversely, when string lengths happen to be\n4-byte aligned, the reservation is too large and stale buffer content\nis sent to the client.\n\nFix this by breaking out every encoded field explicitly in the ds_len\ncalculation, using xdr_align_size() for all variable-length opaque\nfields, and correcting the header constants.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:50:47", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a7fd224df0fbb42167eb1b77be45d72fe0b1098", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29e4478e2ed5a227e8f0c33cacb91bf227cedd47", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65a72b721943618eeb3a41c8b36e915591f3f83f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bee826c00ac900473f91306f1f3e5a5a81fd4a74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7d9d23ecd9172f05b09bb678ff22db8e361c428", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0380129b1373c437eb35401a174671c8888f4b80", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c81cef6a805dec266c10fc4f83c93d6fcf1a2b43", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9868174af49d207fbaf0c5e055d088a983684af"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qhmp-vm7x-v422", "CVE-2026-89674"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.51, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02163d87-9410-3508-bc22-4831ba2be670", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "030979e1-d0b5-33cc-b8c6-1c34a60b38c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "11f73456-ecc1-38af-9bb9-58d58065d63f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, {"id": "26506771-42fa-34e1-a9db-35ea9a05b630", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9b9960a0ca4773e21c4b153ed355583946346b25 <c81cef6a805dec266c10fc4f83c93d6fcf1a2b43"}, {"id": "347937c4-b7f6-32c5-ad87-6cb75c55f511", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "43580efb-9db8-3f60-8e69-ee85a6ee82f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9b9960a0ca4773e21c4b153ed355583946346b25 <bee826c00ac900473f91306f1f3e5a5a81fd4a74"}, {"id": "4c434fc7-c1df-3bc8-9226-88bf0ce0cac2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "5ac224ac-14ba-370b-8543-73847f8b0adf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9b9960a0ca4773e21c4b153ed355583946346b25 <29e4478e2ed5a227e8f0c33cacb91bf227cedd47"}, {"id": "6ffb0f1f-b188-3b35-a3b0-01b45830a1df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "798ef5ff-ce52-38fc-a1cb-a6189d62834e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9b9960a0ca4773e21c4b153ed355583946346b25 <e7d9d23ecd9172f05b09bb678ff22db8e361c428"}, {"id": "7c35633b-13ef-31b6-9b24-3c60315861ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name":